{"step_index":268,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:04:54Z","thinking":"**Applying minimum membership property**\n\n`Finset.mem_of_min` provides the core insight needed: if a set's minimum equals some element `a`, then `a` is in the set. Since the minimum value `s.min` is related to `a`, `s.min.getD 0 = a` also implies `a` is in the set. Specifically for a nonempty set, the `Finset.min_of_mem` rule guarantees the existence of such an `a`, leading to the conclusion that `s.min.getD 0` is an element of `s`.\n\nConsidering the `romanDominationNumber G` expression, it's defined as `(((univ.filter (IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image romanWeight).min).getD 0`. Let `S` represent the set `(univ.filter (IsRoman`.\n\n\n**Deriving Roman Domination Number**\n\nThe `romanDominationNumber` of `G` is the weight of some Roman dominating function `f` applied to the graph. This is derived using `Finset.min_of_mem`, `Finset.mem_of_min`, `Finset.mem_image`, and `Finset.mem_filter`. Specifically, since `romanDominationNumber G = a`, and `a` is a member of the image of a filter, then there exists `f` where the weight of that `f` equals the Roman domination number.\n\n**Analyzing Graph Radius**\n\nExamining `radius G` involves the set `E` which is the image of `eccentricity G` over all vertices. Because for any vertex `v`, its `eccentricity` is a member of `E`, the minimum element in `E` is less than or equal to the eccentricity of `v`. The definition of `radius` then reveals that `radius G` is less than or equal to `eccentricity G v` for all vertices.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport subprocess, os, tempfile\n\ndef check_lean(code):\n    envf = '/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/.agf_env'\n    with open(envf) as f:\n        for line in f:\n            if line.startswith('AGF_ELAN_HOME='):\n                elan_home = line.strip().split('=', 1)[1]\n    lean = os.path.join(elan_home, 'bin/lean')\n    with open('/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/.agf_lean_path') as f:\n        lp = f.read().strip()\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env['ELAN_HOME'] = elan_home\n    env['LEAN_PATH'] = lp\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix='.lean', mode='w', delete=False) as tf:\n        tf.write(code)\n        tf_path = tf.name\n    res = subprocess.run([lean, tf_path], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)\n    os.unlink(tf_path)\n    return res.stdout, res.stderr, res.returncode\n\ncode = '''\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\n  rw [hb]\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\n    Finset.min_le hmem\n  rw [hb] at hle\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\n'''\nout, err, rc = check_lean(code)\nprint('stdout:\\n', out)\nprint('stderr:\\n', err)\nprint('rc:', rc)\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":30000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Test radius_le_eccentricity lemma in Lean"}}]}
